                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "188ef9d1-d1b6-385d-a260-6d634a1213dd",
                        "entry_id": "0668e4d8-8061-3295-bc91-09134fafa4f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Furtive, stealthy or catlike."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "57c2940c-022c-4b23-98a4-ef5589334dd8",
                                "sense_id": "188ef9d1-d1b6-385d-a260-6d634a1213dd",
                                "text": "“But of all the awful, second-rate girls I ever met, she’s the worst! […] She’s a sly, creepy, slinky, made-up, insincere vampire! She’s common! She’s awful! She’s a cat!”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da6908dd-aeb7-4178-b077-c71e506cb9bd",
                                "sense_id": "188ef9d1-d1b6-385d-a260-6d634a1213dd",
                                "text": "The concert touched on all this. You could sense history in the various dances of the pianists’ left hands: the slinky syncopations of habanera; the manic but metronomic bounce, in swing, as if between two trampolines."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "89de3166-60b8-3a7b-b63a-155922f71598",
                        "entry_id": "0668e4d8-8061-3295-bc91-09134fafa4f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Thin; lank; lean."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Northumbria",
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7425fcaf-6e3f-4305-82b2-93718f884fa0",
                                "sense_id": "89de3166-60b8-3a7b-b63a-155922f71598",
                                "text": "Do you see that are tall, limber-timbered, slinky-lookin' man with the blue cloak and two long black cords a-hangin' from it with almighty big tassels a-danglin' to the eend^([sic]) of it like the lamp-rope there, a-carryin' part of the cloak folded on one arm like a Roman senator, and t'other arm kimber, with his hat cockaded military like?--well, that is General Conrad Corncob."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e7ec00e-7b9f-4f38-a279-988cbbfbef6c",
                                "sense_id": "89de3166-60b8-3a7b-b63a-155922f71598",
                                "text": "\"Oh--that,\" said Mrs. Savaker, jerking her head in the direction of the defunct exciseman; \"that war my husband, and war thow't a gude likeness. But it's not. It's not half red enough, an a deal too slinky in the should for him.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dc23b377-3a7e-399c-86d7-1dc49a95bbfe",
                        "entry_id": "0668e4d8-8061-3295-bc91-09134fafa4f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of a garment: close-fitting; clingy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2db8ee9-d159-4fa0-b2a7-732d67cf0fea",
                                "sense_id": "dc23b377-3a7e-399c-86d7-1dc49a95bbfe",
                                "text": "The double-breasted blazer which is on every front row this season came with an elbow-length sleeve for spring, while jumpsuits, a signature of the label, came slinky and tailored or in a blowsier boiler suit silhouette."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
